{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.48.47.201","IsFirstPost":true,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78914,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":12,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"17d9be005a884a970dc368a3831b1337","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:18px;\"&gt;249 till Punta Cana, 254 til the wedding day&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/em&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I\u2019m going to start my Planning thread now...a tad bit early but I figure it will keep me on track...and help me pick up on things I\u2019m forgetting!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we met:&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;We went to same university, took the same classes but never met until years later when we both went back to school for the same program at collage. We both had long term significant others when we started school however just before the last of the 2&lt;sup&gt;nd&lt;\/sup&gt; term started we both happened to be single for the first time in a long time. He asked me out for Coffee and the rest is History! That was April 2006.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n\n&lt;div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:80411]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Some Weird and not so Weird Facts About us:&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;We are the same age...I\u2019m exactly 1 month older&lt;\/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;We are both from Newfoundland Canada, but from total opposite ends of the Island (I\u2019m North and he\u2019s South)&lt;\/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;We are huge Blue Jays Fans&lt;\/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;We have lived together for 8 of our 9 years together.&lt;\/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;We love looking for beach glass in the summer&lt;\/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;We love camping, Fishing, Ice Fishing,&lt;\/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;We both had the same Wayne Gretzky Barbie Doll (action figure if you ask my FI) when we were little.&lt;\/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Our Song is \u201cHot Legs\u201d by Rod Stewart, and it\u2019s a long story as to why&lt;\/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;We have the same Favorite color \u2013 Bright cobalt Blue&lt;\/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;We both love peanut butter on our French toast.&lt;\/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;We have two cats...sisters from the same litter \u201cChewy\u201d the black one and \u201cDitto\u201d the white one.&lt;\/li&gt;\n&lt;\/ul&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:80412]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Proposal:&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:11pt;\"&gt;We have always considered April Fools our Anniversary and so on our 7&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;\/sup&gt; anniversary I woke him up super early and gave him his card. My card had a super mushy and heartfelt letter inside, because we had gone through our first and only (so far...fingers crossed...lol) \u201cRough Patch\u201d just a few months previous and I had wanted to tell him how I felt. He got all emotional (which he does not do) and started blabbering on about how lucky we are and how we are going to staying together forever and have babies and get old. He told me we wanted to marry me. Now I went to work like I normally would...and I just assumed he was talking shit because I had woke him up REALLY early and hit him with that letter before his coffee! Haha! That afternoon he picked me up from work that afternoon but instead of going home we went to a jewellery store and he told me to pick out a ring because he meant every word he had said in the morning. So not a typical planned proposal story...but it\u2019s our story and I love it.&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:80413]&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Plan:&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;So my FI is not keen on weddings in general, he has severe phobia of talking in front of people...so for him the smaller the wedding the better. My FI was also what you call an \u201cAccident\u201d, His parents came home from a holiday with a surprise...ha...so his brothers and sisters are my Parents age and his mom and dad are more like my grandparents age...so Needless to say even though we are both Newfoundlanders we had totally different up bringing! His dream wedding would be just him and I and maybe our parents at city hall...that\u2019s it!&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;But me on the other hand I LOVE weddings! My mom owned a craft store, where I spent all my time!&amp;nbsp; It was a very small town so our craft store also sold wedding supplies, wedding magazines...and my mom made wedding dresses. So let\u2019s just say I\u2019ve been thinking about my wedding for a very LONG long long time. I had multiple Pinterest wedding boards for many years now... before Pinterest was even popular! I also love hanging out with all my family, aunts, uncles, cousins...and I get terribly homesick, there is no better smell than ocean air...I\u2019m a sook! My Dream wedding be a giant wedding at home in my small town with everyone I know...all of our family, friends, extended family, outside near the ocean...lots of dancing, music, food drinks, speeches...I love the speeches...lol...obviously this was not going to fly.&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;We had a limited budget because we are paying for the wedding ourselves, with just a little help...my Parents offered to give us the same amount that they paid for their wedding when they got married almost 40years ago ($5000 ), that was actually a HUGE help...just about doubled our budget! We knew a Toronto wedding was out of the question...way too expensive...and I needed to be near the ocean! I wanted to invite all my Family but my FI wanted something much smaller.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;We thought a destination wedding would be perfect!&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;Ocean...Check!&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;Could invite a ton of people on a small budget (this is before we realised you still pay by the person)...Check!&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;Nice weather...Check!&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;Spend a whole week with the people we love and miss....Check!&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:11pt;\"&gt;People who weren\u2019t totally close to you probably would not go....Check!&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/li&gt;\n&lt;\/ul&gt;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:80414]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Resort:&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:11pt;\"&gt;We knew where immediately...The Grand Palladium in Punta Cana! We had gone there for our first Vacation together right after graduation...we had an awesome time! Since we had been there before it was a bit more comforting to me...I wouldn\u2019t want to take everyone I love to a place new place that I know nothing about and could be awful!&amp;nbsp; I looked up the Wedding Packages...they seemed reasonable; this was also before I knew about extras. I looked up the flights on a bunch of different carriers...again seemed reasonable. It was Family Friendly too which was great since a lot of our friends have kids now. This resort is huge...I wanted to make sure that people who&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:15px;\"&gt;didn&#039;t&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-size:11pt;\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;want to spend more money on excursions would not get bored at the resort. There are tons of restaurants &amp;amp; Bars, daily activities...so there is something for everyone! In the end the wedding package end up being a lot more than I thought, and so did the All-inclusive package, but still somewhat manageable with our budget. I am happy with my Resort pick so far...my WC is great so far, and I\u2019ve heard nothing but great things about her from the other brides on here so that\u2019s great. If I had my time back though, I would have done a little more research on this resort and others...my bad.&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:80415]&amp;nbsp;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:80416]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Date:&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;No question... April Fools 2015! It was the day of our first date. It was the day we got engaged. April is a good time to go to Punta Cana! And who gets married on April Fools on Wednesday! We do!&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;So I did what the resort website said and I emailed the resort and put down my deposit before I sorted my travel just to make sure the date was available...the date was ours!&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Fall-Out:&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;This is where the plan went to shit! Lol!&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;First of all we have to tell everyone. I had prepared myself for the \u201cwhy don\u2019t you just come home and get married...\u201d plea from friends and family. Which totally happened, and I felt guilty as heck even though I knew it was coming, but this was our compromise so I stuck to it. Every time I spoke to my Nan I would feel guilty and cry...she used every guilt trick in the book...god I love her! Lol! But I stuck to my guns!&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;Next, get a TA and a travel package. For the US ladies, in Canada we get an All-Inclusive package at a group rate, this covers Flight down and back, airport transfers, and your all inclusive stay at the resort...and most of the time everyone travels together, you also get bonus\u2019 like 11&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;\/sup&gt; person to book gets a free package...etc. &amp;nbsp;I went to a wedding show and got several TA names and Destination Wedding Travel agency contacts. I emailed, and no one really responded...and one people who did were very pushy and abrasive wanted money right away to secure their \u201cservices\u201d...Alarm Bells! So I got the name of Travel Agent from one of the lovely ladies here on BDW forum. She was great at first but before we got things settled and booked she disappeared!&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;While the TA was MIA a few other personal things happened from Jun to Aug ...My FI got into small car accident...no one was hurt, but it ate into our budget.&amp;nbsp; My Mom got laid off so she was unsure if they could&amp;nbsp;honour&amp;nbsp;their offer to help with the budget. Our close Friend \/ Neighbour got pancreatic cancer and passed away, My FI\u2019s Sister in California got a very aggressive liver cancer and passed away a very short time thereafter. My Nan was also diagnosed with bone cancer...head to toe. I had started having anxiety and small panic attacks...which totally freaked me out because I am so normally laidback; my FI is usually the high strung one.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;When the fog cleared the wedding date was now too close, we had no travel, no TA, no plans, no money, the whole family was still kind of stressed...so we decided to postpone. What\u2019s another year if we\u2019ve been together this long.&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The New Date:&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;We decided to pick a new date since April turned out to be pretty expensive because it was high season. We wanted to get married in 2015 and my FI\u2019s Work does not allow vacay in December so we picked the last week of November. &amp;nbsp;I emailed the resort and I was able to switch my wedding date to Nov 25th and keep my deposit!&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;My New TA:&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;I decided I\u2019ve had enough of calling and emailing...I wanted someone I could talk to face to face, who couldn\u2019t ignore me or disappear! I walked into the flight centre next to my work and got the manager. She has been awesome! We have had so much trouble with our travel package it has been unbelievable! She has even said she\u2019s never seen anything like it! But she fought with the airline for me and got me everything they had promised!&amp;nbsp; The Guaranteed price booking deadline has since passed and we have 44 people, so far. Now to wait til Sept when final payments are due.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Legal Wedding:&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;We decided to have our legal wedding in Newfoundland in July. Just us, our Parents, and my Nan\u2019s. My two Nans will be our witness\u2019. Mark Parents are pretty old and after all the stress of the past summer&amp;nbsp;their&amp;nbsp;health was up and down so we decided that this would be a good back up in case something were to happen and they could not make the trip. Also&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;I really wanted my Nan to be a part of my wedding, but since her diagnoses she was told not to travel out of country and she cannot get travel insurance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;Side note about my Nan...she is the strongest woman I know...I swear she lives on pure spite! She is currently 87...has had breast cancer twice and now full on bone cancer! Never took a treatment of any kind and is still going strong. She lives alone, cooks &amp;amp; bakes, makes bread, Gardens both flowers and vegetables, &amp;nbsp;shovels her driveway, packs up wood for her furnace, she still drives (very well I might add) and takes her neighbours who don\u2019t have a car 20min to the nearest town for Dr apts. She is so AWESOME! And I can\u2019t imagine my day without her.&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;We are unsure about the details exactly yet...but we soon have to figure that out...We will use the Punta Cana Wedding date as our Anniversary Date and we are keeping the legal wedding a secret,&amp;nbsp;although&amp;nbsp;I&#039;m sure no one will care.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Coming Soon...The Dress...Shoes...Jewellery...and other fun inspirations :)&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1889409,"PostDate":1426520729,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p><em><span  style=\"font-size:18px\">249 till Punta Cana, 254 til the wedding day<\/span><\/em><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I\u2019m going to start my Planning thread now...a tad bit early but I figure it will keep me on track...and help me pick up on things I\u2019m forgetting!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong>How we met:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>We went to same university, took the same classes but never met until years later when we both went back to school for the same program at collage. We both had long term significant others when we started school however just before the last of the 2<sup>nd<\/sup> term started we both happened to be single for the first time in a long time. He asked me out for Coffee and the rest is History! That was April 2006.\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<br><div>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/80411-img-4348\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17981\/sml_gallery_268499_17981_11664.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='IMG 4348'  width='200' height='200'  alt='IMG 4348' id='sml_image_view_80411' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<p><strong>Some Weird and not so Weird Facts About us:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul><li>We are the same age...I\u2019m exactly 1 month older<\/li>\n<li>We are both from Newfoundland Canada, but from total opposite ends of the Island (I\u2019m North and he\u2019s South)<\/li>\n<li>We are huge Blue Jays Fans<\/li>\n<li>We have lived together for 8 of our 9 years together.<\/li>\n<li>We love looking for beach glass in the summer<\/li>\n<li>We love camping, Fishing, Ice Fishing,<\/li>\n<li>We both had the same Wayne Gretzky Barbie Doll (action figure if you ask my FI) when we were little.<\/li>\n<li>Our Song is \u201cHot Legs\u201d by Rod Stewart, and it\u2019s a long story as to why<\/li>\n<li>We have the same Favorite color \u2013 Bright cobalt Blue<\/li>\n<li>We both love peanut butter on our French toast.<\/li>\n<li>We have two cats...sisters from the same litter \u201cChewy\u201d the black one and \u201cDitto\u201d the white one.<\/li>\n<\/ul><div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/80412-img-0211\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17981\/sml_gallery_268499_17981_140518.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='IMG 0211'  width='200' height='200'  alt='IMG 0211' id='sml_image_view_80412' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><strong>The Proposal:<\/strong><\/span><\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:11pt\">We have always considered April Fools our Anniversary and so on our 7<sup>th<\/sup> anniversary I woke him up super early and gave him his card. My card had a super mushy and heartfelt letter inside, because we had gone through our first and only (so far...fingers crossed...lol) \u201cRough Patch\u201d just a few months previous and I had wanted to tell him how I felt. He got all emotional (which he does not do) and started blabbering on about how lucky we are and how we are going to staying together forever and have babies and get old. He told me we wanted to marry me. Now I went to work like I normally would...and I just assumed he was talking shit because I had woke him up REALLY early and hit him with that letter before his coffee! Haha! That afternoon he picked me up from work that afternoon but instead of going home we went to a jewellery store and he told me to pick out a ring because he meant every word he had said in the morning. So not a typical planned proposal story...but it\u2019s our story and I love it.<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<div><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/80413-483745-10151310103916890-2108487317-n\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17981\/sml_gallery_268499_17981_16666.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='483745 10151310103916890 2108487317 N'  width='200' height='200'  alt='483745 10151310103916890 2108487317 N' id='sml_image_view_80413' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/span><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><strong>The Plan:<\/strong><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">So my FI is not keen on weddings in general, he has severe phobia of talking in front of people...so for him the smaller the wedding the better. My FI was also what you call an \u201cAccident\u201d, His parents came home from a holiday with a surprise...ha...so his brothers and sisters are my Parents age and his mom and dad are more like my grandparents age...so Needless to say even though we are both Newfoundlanders we had totally different up bringing! His dream wedding would be just him and I and maybe our parents at city hall...that\u2019s it!<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">But me on the other hand I LOVE weddings! My mom owned a craft store, where I spent all my time!\u00a0 It was a very small town so our craft store also sold wedding supplies, wedding magazines...and my mom made wedding dresses. So let\u2019s just say I\u2019ve been thinking about my wedding for a very LONG long long time. I had multiple Pinterest wedding boards for many years now... before Pinterest was even popular! I also love hanging out with all my family, aunts, uncles, cousins...and I get terribly homesick, there is no better smell than ocean air...I\u2019m a sook! My Dream wedding be a giant wedding at home in my small town with everyone I know...all of our family, friends, extended family, outside near the ocean...lots of dancing, music, food drinks, speeches...I love the speeches...lol...obviously this was not going to fly.<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">We had a limited budget because we are paying for the wedding ourselves, with just a little help...my Parents offered to give us the same amount that they paid for their wedding when they got married almost 40years ago ($5000 ), that was actually a HUGE help...just about doubled our budget! We knew a Toronto wedding was out of the question...way too expensive...and I needed to be near the ocean! I wanted to invite all my Family but my FI wanted something much smaller.\u00a0<\/span><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">We thought a destination wedding would be perfect!<\/span><\/p>\n<ul><li><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Ocean...Check!<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Could invite a ton of people on a small budget (this is before we realised you still pay by the person)...Check!<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Nice weather...Check!<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Spend a whole week with the people we love and miss....Check!<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span  style=\"font-size:11pt\">People who weren\u2019t totally close to you probably would not go....Check!<\/span><\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/80414-jam-rock-2013\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17981\/sml_gallery_268499_17981_33319.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='Jam Rock 2013'  width='200' height='150'  alt='Jam Rock 2013' id='sml_image_view_80414' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><strong>The Resort:<\/strong><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-size:11pt\">We knew where immediately...The Grand Palladium in Punta Cana! We had gone there for our first Vacation together right after graduation...we had an awesome time! Since we had been there before it was a bit more comforting to me...I wouldn\u2019t want to take everyone I love to a place new place that I know nothing about and could be awful!\u00a0 I looked up the Wedding Packages...they seemed reasonable; this was also before I knew about extras. I looked up the flights on a bunch of different carriers...again seemed reasonable. It was Family Friendly too which was great since a lot of our friends have kids now. This resort is huge...I wanted to make sure that people who\u00a0<\/span><span  style=\"font-size:15px\">didn't<\/span><span  style=\"font-size:11pt\">\u00a0want to spend more money on excursions would not get bored at the resort. There are tons of restaurants & Bars, daily activities...so there is something for everyone! In the end the wedding package end up being a lot more than I thought, and so did the All-inclusive package, but still somewhat manageable with our budget. I am happy with my Resort pick so far...my WC is great so far, and I\u2019ve heard nothing but great things about her from the other brides on here so that\u2019s great. If I had my time back though, I would have done a little more research on this resort and others...my bad.<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<div><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/80415-punta-cana-2007\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17981\/sml_gallery_268499_17981_344282.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='Punta Cana 2007'  width='200' height='200'  alt='Punta Cana 2007' id='sml_image_view_80415' \/><\/a>\n<br \/>\u00a0<!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/80416-gazebo\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17971\/sml_gallery_268499_17971_61872.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='Gazebo'  width='200' height='121'  alt='Gazebo' id='sml_image_view_80416' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><strong>The Date:<\/strong><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">No question... April Fools 2015! It was the day of our first date. It was the day we got engaged. April is a good time to go to Punta Cana! And who gets married on April Fools on Wednesday! We do!\u00a0<\/span><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">So I did what the resort website said and I emailed the resort and put down my deposit before I sorted my travel just to make sure the date was available...the date was ours!<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><strong>The Fall-Out:<\/strong><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">This is where the plan went to shit! Lol!<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">First of all we have to tell everyone. I had prepared myself for the \u201cwhy don\u2019t you just come home and get married...\u201d plea from friends and family. Which totally happened, and I felt guilty as heck even though I knew it was coming, but this was our compromise so I stuck to it. Every time I spoke to my Nan I would feel guilty and cry...she used every guilt trick in the book...god I love her! Lol! But I stuck to my guns!<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Next, get a TA and a travel package. For the US ladies, in Canada we get an All-Inclusive package at a group rate, this covers Flight down and back, airport transfers, and your all inclusive stay at the resort...and most of the time everyone travels together, you also get bonus\u2019 like 11<sup>th<\/sup> person to book gets a free package...etc. \u00a0I went to a wedding show and got several TA names and Destination Wedding Travel agency contacts. I emailed, and no one really responded...and one people who did were very pushy and abrasive wanted money right away to secure their \u201cservices\u201d...Alarm Bells! So I got the name of Travel Agent from one of the lovely ladies here on BDW forum. She was great at first but before we got things settled and booked she disappeared!<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>While the TA was MIA a few other personal things happened from Jun to Aug ...My FI got into small car accident...no one was hurt, but it ate into our budget.\u00a0 My Mom got laid off so she was unsure if they could\u00a0honour\u00a0their offer to help with the budget. Our close Friend \/ Neighbour got pancreatic cancer and passed away, My FI\u2019s Sister in California got a very aggressive liver cancer and passed away a very short time thereafter. My Nan was also diagnosed with bone cancer...head to toe. I had started having anxiety and small panic attacks...which totally freaked me out because I am so normally laidback; my FI is usually the high strung one.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">When the fog cleared the wedding date was now too close, we had no travel, no TA, no plans, no money, the whole family was still kind of stressed...so we decided to postpone. What\u2019s another year if we\u2019ve been together this long.<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><strong>The New Date:<\/strong><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">We decided to pick a new date since April turned out to be pretty expensive because it was high season. We wanted to get married in 2015 and my FI\u2019s Work does not allow vacay in December so we picked the last week of November. \u00a0I emailed the resort and I was able to switch my wedding date to Nov 25th and keep my deposit!<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><strong>My New TA:<\/strong><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">I decided I\u2019ve had enough of calling and emailing...I wanted someone I could talk to face to face, who couldn\u2019t ignore me or disappear! I walked into the flight centre next to my work and got the manager. She has been awesome! We have had so much trouble with our travel package it has been unbelievable! She has even said she\u2019s never seen anything like it! But she fought with the airline for me and got me everything they had promised!\u00a0 The Guaranteed price booking deadline has since passed and we have 44 people, so far. Now to wait til Sept when final payments are due.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><strong>The Legal Wedding:<\/strong><\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We decided to have our legal wedding in Newfoundland in July. Just us, our Parents, and my Nan\u2019s. My two Nans will be our witness\u2019. Mark Parents are pretty old and after all the stress of the past summer\u00a0their\u00a0health was up and down so we decided that this would be a good back up in case something were to happen and they could not make the trip. Also\u00a0<span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">I really wanted my Nan to be a part of my wedding, but since her diagnoses she was told not to travel out of country and she cannot get travel insurance.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Side note about my Nan...she is the strongest woman I know...I swear she lives on pure spite! She is currently 87...has had breast cancer twice and now full on bone cancer! Never took a treatment of any kind and is still going strong. She lives alone, cooks & bakes, makes bread, Gardens both flowers and vegetables, \u00a0shovels her driveway, packs up wood for her furnace, she still drives (very well I might add) and takes her neighbours who don\u2019t have a car 20min to the nearest town for Dr apts. She is so AWESOME! And I can\u2019t imagine my day without her.<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We are unsure about the details exactly yet...but we soon have to figure that out...We will use the Punta Cana Wedding date as our Anniversary Date and we are keeping the legal wedding a secret,\u00a0although\u00a0I'm sure no one will care.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Coming Soon...The Dress...Shoes...Jewellery...and other fun inspirations <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78914-meandhim-grand-palladium-bavaro-nov-2015\/'>My Planning Thread<\/a>\u00a0- MeandHim - Grand Palladium Bavaro - Nov 25 2015<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10765;116\/st\/20151125\/e\/Our+Wedding\/k\/461e\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"markandshavonne@live.com","IpAddress":"70.30.85.211","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1365792059,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-268499.jpg?_r=1395417550","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Meandhim","Id":268499,"Name":"Meandhim","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.72.41.59","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78914,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":2,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"31e06e17b386c84a0551e655e5eff854","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;LOVE!!!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I enjoyed reading your thread!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I also got engaged on April 1st :)&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I am glad thru all of the things that happened to your and your family that you were able to come out the other side with a wedding date!!! &amp;nbsp;November is all that far away now, yay!!!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Your grandma is strong. Cancer is just so awful and it&#039;s enduring to hear that she is alive and kicking and well, kicking it&#039;s a$$ by the sounds of it. &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;can&#039;t wait for more! &amp;nbsp;and ps - your ring is gorgeous!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1889545,"PostDate":1426557525,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>LOVE!!!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I enjoyed reading your thread!<\/p>\n<p>I also got engaged on April 1st <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I am glad thru all of the things that happened to your and your family that you were able to come out the other side with a wedding date!!! \u00a0November is all that far away now, yay!!!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Your grandma is strong. Cancer is just so awful and it's enduring to hear that she is alive and kicking and well, kicking it's a$$ by the sounds of it. \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>can't wait for more! \u00a0and ps - your ring is gorgeous!<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>-Kim<\/p>\n<p>Married on 2015\/01\/21 at the Grand Sirenis Riviera Maya with 43 guests in attendance \u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Planning Thread -\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Pictures\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Review\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"kdeakin@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"68.145.235.0","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1399428602,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277873.jpg?_r=1422218225","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"calgarybride2015","Id":277873,"Name":"calgarybride2015","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"174.117.36.109","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78914,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"59135827e2b1dba6f20bda4db4cb756e","RawContent":"@[member=\"calgarybride2015\"] \n\nthanks :) I&#039;m glad you liked it! I hope to have a more fun planning post sometime this week! \n\n\nApril Fools is my favourite day of the year! I think Its a lucky day for fools in love :)\n\n\nNovember is feeling pretty close right now!! I feel like I&#039;m behind!!! I think I need to tackle the details for the legal ceremony first since that&#039;s coming up so soon!  \n\n\n My Nan does kick a$$...lol.\n\n\nI love my ring! But hey I picked it out.. Haha! It actually looks a lot bigger in that picture than it is. The smaller the better for me tho ... I rarely wear jewellery.\n\n\n\n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk","Attachments":[],"Id":1889568,"PostDate":1426559668,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                @<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"277873\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/277873-calgarybride2015\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">calgarybride2015<\/span><\/a> <br>\nthanks <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> I'm glad you liked it! I hope to have a more fun planning post sometime this week! <br><br>\nApril Fools is my favourite day of the year! I think Its a lucky day for fools in love <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><br><br>\nNovember is feeling pretty close right now!! I feel like I'm behind!!! I think I need to tackle the details for the legal ceremony first since that's coming up so soon!  <br><br>\n My Nan does kick a$$...lol.<br><br>\nI love my ring! But hey I picked it out.. Haha! It actually looks a lot bigger in that picture than it is. The smaller the better for me tho ... I rarely wear jewellery.<br><br><br><br><br>\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78914-meandhim-grand-palladium-bavaro-nov-2015\/'>My Planning Thread<\/a>\u00a0- MeandHim - Grand Palladium Bavaro - Nov 25 2015<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10765;116\/st\/20151125\/e\/Our+Wedding\/k\/461e\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"markandshavonne@live.com","IpAddress":"70.30.85.211","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1365792059,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-268499.jpg?_r=1395417550","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Meandhim","Id":268499,"Name":"Meandhim","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.72.41.59","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78914,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"944bc5a879ff12017f065159b02bd4af","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;I may have said to husband &#039;is this an April Fool&#039;s joke? &#039; heheheh&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Mine isn&#039;t that large either. &amp;nbsp; I told husband way way before we got engaged that I would rather spend the money on something else. That I didn&#039;t need anything large and elaborate. &amp;nbsp;Ok sure I wouldn&#039;t mind it but LOVE my ring (which in the end I also picked) and wouldn&#039;t change it for the world!!&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1889571,"PostDate":1426559882,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>I may have said to husband 'is this an April Fool's joke? ' heheheh<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Mine isn't that large either. \u00a0 I told husband way way before we got engaged that I would rather spend the money on something else. That I didn't need anything large and elaborate. \u00a0Ok sure I wouldn't mind it but LOVE my ring (which in the end I also picked) and wouldn't change it for the world!!\u00a0<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>-Kim<\/p>\n<p>Married on 2015\/01\/21 at the Grand Sirenis Riviera Maya with 43 guests in attendance \u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Planning Thread -\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Pictures\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Review\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"kdeakin@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"68.145.235.0","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1399428602,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277873.jpg?_r=1422218225","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"calgarybride2015","Id":277873,"Name":"calgarybride2015","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"137.186.96.83","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78914,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"c19c9fef087318ecd1eccffc5834b75c","RawContent":"Oh I am so glad you started your thread. I loved reading your story too.  And yay another Newfoundlander in the planning process. Love it.  And yes I miss the ocean also and I am also a big sook and get home sick especially when listening to the Irish Newdoundland show Sunday mornings. Haha\n\n\nI cannot wait to read more of your planning. I am pretty sure we both joined this site at the same time so it&#039;s more exciting to see you getting closer to your date.","Attachments":[],"Id":1889574,"PostDate":1426561018,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Oh I am so glad you started your thread. I loved reading your story too.  And yay another Newfoundlander in the planning process. Love it.  And yes I miss the ocean also and I am also a big sook and get home sick especially when listening to the Irish Newdoundland show Sunday mornings. Haha<br><br>\nI cannot wait to read more of your planning. I am pretty sure we both joined this site at the same time so it's more exciting to see you getting closer to your date.\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p style=\"text-align:center;\"><strong>Kristy and Nathan<\/strong><\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\"><strong>Melia Caribe Tropical <\/strong><\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\"><strong>April 17, 2015<\/strong>","Email":"colek_64@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"199.180.174.8","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1395346614,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277264.jpg?_r=1429937323","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"kcole123","Id":277264,"Name":"kcole123","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"96.48.159.21","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78914,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"f51e143500267a6f743b6cdf03add210","RawContent":"@[member=\"Meandhim\"] I love your planning thread. I love your honesty, your perseverance and your love for your family.\n\n\nI commend your Nan for being such a strong woman. Cancer sucks and has hit me close to home, my dad died of intestinal cancer and my mom has had breast cancer (thank God she&#039;s all clear now). \n\n\nI can&#039;t wait to read more about your planning!","Attachments":[],"Id":1889580,"PostDate":1426561775,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                @<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"268499\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/268499-meandhim\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">Meandhim<\/span><\/a> I love your planning thread. I love your honesty, your perseverance and your love for your family.<br><br>\nI commend your Nan for being such a strong woman. Cancer sucks and has hit me close to home, my dad died of intestinal cancer and my mom has had breast cancer (thank God she's all clear now). <br><br>\nI can't wait to read more about your planning! \r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"My planning thread: <a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79425-wafflesmom-moon-palace-planning-thread-january-23-2016\/\">http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79425-wafflesmom-moon-palace-planning-thread-january-23-2016\/<\/a><br><br>\n<p><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;4;484\/st\/20160123\/e\/Our+Wedding\/dt\/-2\/k\/44c5\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a>","Email":"jerilee.valenzuela@shaw.ca","IpAddress":"24.114.26.77","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1410098585,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-279721.jpg?_r=1444491864","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Wafflesmom","Id":279721,"Name":"Wafflesmom","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"207.219.69.132","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78914,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"9b0ad8c7bef5c23a7ed25268e0de6dd9","RawContent":"[quote name=\"kcole123\" post=\"1889574\" timestamp=\"1426561018\"]\nOh I am so glad you started your thread. I loved reading your story too.  And yay another Newfoundlander in the planning process. Love it.  And yes I miss the ocean also and I am also a big sook and get home sick especially when listening to the Irish Newdoundland show Sunday mornings. Haha\n\nI cannot wait to read more of your planning. I am pretty sure we both joined this site at the same time so it&#039;s more exciting to see you getting closer to your date.[\/quote]We did join close to the same time and if I had kept my original date I would be leaving for punta cana in 11 days! \n\n[quote name=\"Wafflesmom\" post=\"1889580\" timestamp=\"1426561775\"]\n@[member=\"Meandhim\"] I love your planning thread. I love your honesty, your perseverance and your love for your family.\n\nI commend your Nan for being such a strong woman. Cancer sucks and has hit me close to home, my dad died of intestinal cancer and my mom has had breast cancer (thank God she&#039;s all clear now). \n\nI can&#039;t wait to read more about your planning![\/quote]Thanks :) I do love my family! Sorry to hear about your dad :( and your mom! I&#039;m a little slow with the planning so I&#039;m hoping to have another post soon... Little more of the fun stuff :)\n\n\n[quote name=\"calgarybride2015\" post=\"1889571\" timestamp=\"1426559882\"]\nI may have said to husband &#039;is this an April Fool&#039;s joke? &#039; heheheh\n\nMine isn&#039;t that large either.   I told husband way way before we got engaged that I would rather spend the money on something else. That I didn&#039;t need anything large and elaborate.  Ok sure I wouldn&#039;t mind it but LOVE my ring (which in the end I also picked) and wouldn&#039;t change it for the world!![\/quote]Sometimes I think rings you pick out yourself are better... Lol... After we bought my ring He showed me the one he was going to buy... It was way more expensive, and bigger.. it was nice but I didn&#039;t love it like my ring!\n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk","Attachments":[],"Id":1889783,"PostDate":1426640541,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>kcole123, on 16 March 2015 - 06:56 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'><p>Oh I am so glad you started your thread. I loved reading your story too.  And yay another Newfoundlander in the planning process. Love it.  And yes I miss the ocean also and I am also a big sook and get home sick especially when listening to the Irish Newdoundland show Sunday mornings. Haha<br><br>\nI cannot wait to read more of your planning. I am pretty sure we both joined this site at the same time so it's more exciting to see you getting closer to your date.<\/p><\/div><\/div>\n<br>\nWe did join close to the same time and if I had kept my original date I would be leaving for punta cana in 11 days! <br><br><p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>Wafflesmom, on 16 March 2015 - 07:09 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'><p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"268499\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/268499-meandhim\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">Meandhim<\/span><\/a> I love your planning thread. I love your honesty, your perseverance and your love for your family.<br><br>\nI commend your Nan for being such a strong woman. Cancer sucks and has hit me close to home, my dad died of intestinal cancer and my mom has had breast cancer (thank God she's all clear now). <br><br>\nI can't wait to read more about your planning!<\/p><\/div><\/div>\n<br>\nThanks <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> I do love my family! Sorry to hear about your dad <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/sad.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':(' \/> and your mom! I'm a little slow with the planning so I'm hoping to have another post soon... Little more of the fun stuff <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><br><br><br><p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>calgarybride2015, on 16 March 2015 - 06:38 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'><p>I may have said to husband 'is this an April Fool's joke? ' heheheh<br><br>\nMine isn't that large either.   I told husband way way before we got engaged that I would rather spend the money on something else. That I didn't need anything large and elaborate.  Ok sure I wouldn't mind it but LOVE my ring (which in the end I also picked) and wouldn't change it for the world!!<\/p><\/div><\/div>\n<br>\nSometimes I think rings you pick out yourself are better... Lol... After we bought my ring He showed me the one he was going to buy... It was way more expensive, and bigger.. it was nice but I didn't love it like my ring!<br><br><br>\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78914-meandhim-grand-palladium-bavaro-nov-2015\/'>My Planning Thread<\/a>\u00a0- MeandHim - Grand Palladium Bavaro - Nov 25 2015<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10765;116\/st\/20151125\/e\/Our+Wedding\/k\/461e\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"markandshavonne@live.com","IpAddress":"70.30.85.211","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1365792059,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-268499.jpg?_r=1395417550","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Meandhim","Id":268499,"Name":"Meandhim","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.48.47.201","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78914,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":4,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"7e7930d018db5d2bf55bd8f908edfaa8","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;So yesterday was my&amp;nbsp;favourite&amp;nbsp;day :) as you might know if you read my first post. It would of been my wedding day had we not postponed! It is kind of crazy to think about! I can&#039;t even imagine!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;It was also a special day for @[member=\"calgarybride2015\"] (Happy Engagement Anniversary!) and @[member=\"snswedding2016\"] (Happy 4th Anniversary!) Hope you girls had a great day!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;We celebrated our 9th Anniversary last night...No biggy! We grabbed a burger and went to a movie, He got me flowers and I got him my regular mushy card...our usual..lol. It&amp;nbsp;certainly&amp;nbsp;doesn&#039;t feel like 9 years...feels like no time! I guess that&#039;s a really good thing.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;We decided last night that since next year will be our 10 year&amp;nbsp;anniversary&amp;nbsp;we should probably up the ante..ha! we don&#039;t have enough vacay time left to have honeymoon right after the wedding... so we will take our honeymoon around April Fools next year and celebrate our 10years while on honeymoon!.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;It will be about 4 Months after our wedding in punta cana, we are thinking Negril (Sunset at the Palms) Because we loved it so much or try somewhere we have never been like St. Lucia. I would love to do&amp;nbsp;Greece, or a cruise but we&amp;nbsp;are thinking down south because we have never gone alone, we have always gone with a group, and we wont have a lot of money to play with after the wedding and Christmas! We are open to other ideas...any suggestions?&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I swear I will post more Planning this weekend! I was doing a lot of spring cleaning and buying stuff :)...Update coming soon!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1891707,"PostDate":1428002531,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>So yesterday was my\u00a0favourite\u00a0day <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> as you might know if you read my first post. It would of been my wedding day had we not postponed! It is kind of crazy to think about! I can't even imagine!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>It was also a special day for @<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"277873\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/277873-calgarybride2015\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">calgarybride2015<\/span><\/a> (Happy Engagement Anniversary!) and @<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"281055\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/281055-snswedding2016\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">snswedding2016<\/span><\/a> (Happy 4th Anniversary!) Hope you girls had a great day!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We celebrated our 9th Anniversary last night...No biggy! We grabbed a burger and went to a movie, He got me flowers and I got him my regular mushy card...our usual..lol. It\u00a0certainly\u00a0doesn't feel like 9 years...feels like no time! I guess that's a really good thing.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>We decided last night that since next year will be our 10 year\u00a0anniversary\u00a0we should probably up the ante..ha! we don't have enough vacay time left to have honeymoon right after the wedding... so we will take our honeymoon around April Fools next year and celebrate our 10years while on honeymoon!.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>It will be about 4 Months after our wedding in punta cana, we are thinking Negril (Sunset at the Palms) Because we loved it so much or try somewhere we have never been like St. Lucia. I would love to do\u00a0Greece, or a cruise but we\u00a0are thinking down south because we have never gone alone, we have always gone with a group, and we wont have a lot of money to play with after the wedding and Christmas! We are open to other ideas...any suggestions?<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I swear I will post more Planning this weekend! I was doing a lot of spring cleaning and buying stuff <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>...Update coming soon!<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78914-meandhim-grand-palladium-bavaro-nov-2015\/'>My Planning Thread<\/a>\u00a0- MeandHim - Grand Palladium Bavaro - Nov 25 2015<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10765;116\/st\/20151125\/e\/Our+Wedding\/k\/461e\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"markandshavonne@live.com","IpAddress":"70.30.85.211","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1365792059,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-268499.jpg?_r=1395417550","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Meandhim","Id":268499,"Name":"Meandhim","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"184.149.182.226","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78914,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"89b968c2a96839c420783799c81eb389","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"Meandhim\"] Happy 9th Anniversary!!!! I hope you and your fiance had a nice celebration! :)&amp;nbsp;A honeymoon next April sounds like a perfect way to celebrate 10 years!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1891710,"PostDate":1428004247,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"268499\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/268499-meandhim\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">Meandhim<\/span><\/a> Happy 9th Anniversary!!!! I hope you and your fiance had a nice celebration! <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>\u00a0A honeymoon next April sounds like a perfect way to celebrate 10 years!<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>My planning thread -\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78916-snswedding2016-planning-thread-jan-9-2016-azul-fives\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78916-snswedding2016-planning-thread-jan-9-2016-azul-fives\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<div><a class='bbc_url' href='http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/'><\/div>\n<div><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10730;0\/st\/20160109\/e\/Our+Wedding\/k\/9fa9\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/div>\n<div><\/a><\/div>\n","Email":"sean.n.steph2016@gmail.com","IpAddress":"74.12.52.42","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1415547511,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281055.jpg?_r=1415590512","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":150,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"snswedding2016","Id":281055,"Name":"snswedding2016","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.42.29.13","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78914,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"f1f95257bf7d4d664253542ac00da5cc","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Yay planning thread! I have been looking forward to you starting one!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Happy Anniversary! Burger and a movie sounds like most excellent plans!&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I think your engagement story is fantastic. So cute and spontaneous! &amp;nbsp;Must be crazy though to think that yesterday was almost the day. I think its a really sweet that you&#039;ll get to do it in Newfie with the parents and grandparents. I&#039;m picturing a cliff by the seaside for some reason! lol&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Can&#039;t wait to hear about all the rest!(And steal some ideas of course!&amp;nbsp; :ph34r: )&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1891727,"PostDate":1428014670,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Yay planning thread! I have been looking forward to you starting one!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Happy Anniversary! Burger and a movie sounds like most excellent plans!\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I think your engagement story is fantastic. So cute and spontaneous! \u00a0Must be crazy though to think that yesterday was almost the day. I think its a really sweet that you'll get to do it in Newfie with the parents and grandparents. I'm picturing a cliff by the seaside for some reason! lol<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Can't wait to hear about all the rest!(And steal some ideas of course!\u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/ph34r.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':ph34r:' \/> )<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"seriouslyamber@gmail.com","IpAddress":"99.237.87.24","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1420772942,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281649.jpg?_r=1421027393","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Everly","Id":281649,"Name":"Everly","IsOnline":false}}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":264,"TotalPages":27,"CurrentPage":0,"NextPage":10,"PreviousPage":-1,"LastPage":260},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}
